// `min-width 0` on every link in this chain, not just the leaf. A flex item
// defaults to `min-width auto`, which refuses to shrink below its content, so a
// shortfall becomes OVERFLOW of the ancestor rather than compression here. The
// leaf already carried it and that was not enough: measured in the 70px bar,
// `.auction__bid-info` ran 487px of content in a 407px box and the details
// group's right edge sat 79px past where `.auction__bid-actions` begins, so
// `BYE` and `AGE` rendered underneath the bid controls. The two intermediate
// boxes were the ones refusing to shrink; the leaf could not compress while its
// parents would not.
// `overflow hidden` as well as `min-width 0`, because the two answer different
// halves. `min-width 0` lets the BOX shrink; without `overflow hidden` the
// TEXT inside it still paints at full width over whatever follows, and the
// symptom is identical to not having shrunk at all -- measured at a 1280px
// viewport, this box was 224px wide holding 264px of name, printing "PICKETT"
// straight through "MARKET $0". A box-overlap check cannot see it either: the
// boxes tile perfectly while the ink does not. Clipped, the name truncates on
// `.player__name-top`, which already carries `text-overflow: ellipsis`.
.nominated__player
  display flex
  flex 1
  min-width 0
  overflow hidden

  .player__headshot
    border-radius 0

.auction__nominated-player
  flex 1
  display flex
  min-width 0
  // Each detail clips its OWN ink. The group above having `overflow hidden` is
  // not enough and the distinction is easy to get wrong: that one stops the
  // group painting outside itself, while this stops each item painting over the
  // item beside it. At 900px the four labels want about 170px inside a 132px
  // group -- wrapped, which is what they do at that width -- and without this
  // the shortfall came out as MARKET printed through LIVE VALUE rather than as
  // either one being cut off.
  .selected__player-header-item
    min-width 0
    flex 1 1 0
    overflow hidden

// `overflow hidden` as well as `min-width 0`, the same pairing argued for at
// the top of this file and for the same reason: `min-width 0` lets the BOX
// shrink while the text inside keeps painting at full width over whatever
// follows. This box had only the first half, and a nowrap label was all it took
// to expose it -- at a 900px viewport the labels printed through each other and
// through the headshot ("ARKETVA...", "$0$0") while every box still tiled
// perfectly, so a box-overlap check read clean.
.nominated__player-details
  flex 1
  display flex
  min-width 0
  overflow hidden
  padding-top 8px
  font-size 12px
  label
    font-size 10px
    font-family "Inter", "Helvetica", "Arial", sans-serif;
    font-weight 300
    text-transform uppercase
    display block
    padding-bottom 6px

// `Live value` is the only two-word label in this group, and wrapping it puts
// its amount a line below MARKET, BYE and AGE -- the four sit on one baseline or
// the group reads as broken. So it does not wrap, but only from 1024px up.
//
// THE FLOOR IS NOT CAUTION, IT IS A ZONE THAT IS ALREADY BROKEN. Between the
// 799px breakpoint that stacks the bar and roughly 1160px where the bar gains
// its cap, the four labels want about 170px inside a 132px group and the
// shortfall comes out as overlapping ink -- that is true of the old one-word
// `Auction` too, so it is a defect this label inherits rather than causes.
// Holding nowrap above 1024 keeps the squeeze zone exactly as it was instead of
// making it worse, and measured at 1024, 1160, 1280 and 1440 the group needs no
// more room than it already has: `.auction__bar-body` scrollWidth equals its
// clientWidth at every one, so nothing is pushed past the viewport.
@media (min-width 1024px)
  .nominated__player-details label
    white-space nowrap

// THE STATIC PRICE RECEDES AND THE LIVE ONE DOES NOT. The pair reads as one
// number printed twice otherwise -- same size, same weight, same ink, two
// one-word labels. Making `Market` the quiet one is a subtractive distinction:
// it needs no second accent colour in a bar that already spends red on the
// election amount a hundred pixels away, and it puts the emphasis on the number
// that is actually a live claim about what the player is worth right now.
.nominated__detail-market
  color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55)

.nominated__detail-live
  font-weight 600

@media (max-width 799px)
  .auction__nominated-player .player__name-headshot
    overflow hidden
    position absolute
    background rgba(255,255,255,0.8)
    border 1px solid $borderColor
    border-radius 50%
    width 100px
    height 100px
    display flex
    align-items flex-end
    justify-content center
    top -96px
    left 8px

@media (max-width 500px)
  .auction__nominated-player .selected__player-header-item
    padding 4px
    flex 0 0 auto
    min-width 24px
